#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0106 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "*** The batch's ONE ISOLATED DROP_MISSING_KEYS pin. APERIODC is PRESENT (blank on every row) so var_exists(APERIODC) is TRUE, and not empty(APERIOD) is TRUE on every row - no conjunct is false here. The ONLY thing silencing the rule is GroupSemantics.partition discarding every blank-key row under DROP_MISSING_KEYS. The same APERIOD sequence fires when APERIODC is PERIOD1 (see the violation fixture)."
#library standard=adamig version=1-0
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID  type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col PARAMCD  type=Char
col APERIOD  type=Num
col APERIODC type=Char
---
